WEBVTT

00:04.010 --> 00:06.270
I-It's finally almost done, huh?

00:09.440 --> 00:15.410
It's the platinum that Kohaku and
the spy team worked so hard to find!

00:15.410 --> 00:17.620
And now we have the water
of the miracle cave...

00:17.620 --> 00:20.700
Nitric acid
acquired!!

00:18.380 --> 00:20.700
We have nitric acid!

00:21.070 --> 00:22.370
Man...

00:22.370 --> 00:26.670
We were nearly wiped
out 3,700 years ago,

00:26.670 --> 00:32.530
and now on this island,
by that petrification beam...

00:34.600 --> 00:36.780
But now we can unpetrify anyone we want.

00:36.780 --> 00:40.150
In other words, the revival of
humanity is set in stone now.

00:41.290 --> 00:46.020
Kingdom of Science

00:41.290 --> 00:46.020
Petrification Kingdom

00:41.790 --> 00:45.590
It's the start of the Kingdom
of Science's counterattack!

02:16.260 --> 02:20.990
The Kingdom of Science's
Counterattack

02:21.770 --> 02:24.610
Now that we have nitric acid...

02:24.610 --> 02:27.420
Oh, yeah, didn't you mention gunpowder before?

02:27.420 --> 02:29.210
So we can make guns and stuff, right?

02:29.210 --> 02:31.690
There's no way we're making <i>that</i> much.

02:31.690 --> 02:34.880
Maybe if we could construct
a legit factory or something...

02:34.880 --> 02:39.220
Sadly, we're stuck making puny amounts
with janky makeshift equipment.

02:39.220 --> 02:41.310
We're gonna have to go slow.

02:41.310 --> 02:46.140
I guess we can't spend months waiting
to make enough for a war, huh?

02:46.140 --> 02:47.030
That's right.

02:47.030 --> 02:49.450
We aren't waiting. We're going straight in.

02:49.450 --> 02:52.370
We're going to slap our allies
awake as soon as we have

02:52.370 --> 02:55.070
enough revival fluid for each of them.

02:55.550 --> 03:00.820
First off, we're saving our god-tier craftsman,
Kaseki, so he can work on our drone.

03:10.210 --> 03:14.250
Th-They're getting dumped in the water!

03:14.490 --> 03:16.030
Of course they are.

03:16.030 --> 03:19.300
As far as they're concerned,
they're just useless rocks.

03:19.300 --> 03:20.680
Hang on, though.

03:20.680 --> 03:24.420
We couldn't save them if they were in
the middle of a well-guarded war zone,

03:24.420 --> 03:28.000
but this might be an opportunity,
since we can dive down to retrieve them.

03:28.000 --> 03:30.480
I-If we can find them.

03:30.480 --> 03:32.730
Including the bits that'll get washed away.

03:33.010 --> 03:34.610
The water currents...

03:34.610 --> 03:36.190
We need Ryusui, then!

03:37.340 --> 03:39.570
If Ryusui would come back...

03:42.840 --> 03:45.770
His clothes are way too fancy.

03:45.770 --> 03:48.620
He must be the boss.

03:48.620 --> 03:50.030
O-Oh, no!

03:50.030 --> 03:52.530
They took Ryusui with them!

03:54.970 --> 04:00.090
Your uncle's got some
sad news for all of you.

04:00.400 --> 04:04.340
There might be an invader among you.

04:05.050 --> 04:08.010
We're gonna have to flush her out.

04:09.140 --> 04:11.890
If you aren't friends with this statue,

04:11.890 --> 04:15.020
you don't mind us breaking it, right?

04:22.010 --> 04:23.900
Okay, next!

04:24.780 --> 04:26.870
How dare you, you cruel...

04:26.870 --> 04:28.020
No! No!

04:28.020 --> 04:29.100
Hold it back!

04:29.100 --> 04:31.200
Kohaku-chan, don't charge at them!

04:31.200 --> 04:34.980
I mean, it doesn't mean he's dead
even if they break him, right?

04:34.980 --> 04:38.130
He'll come back to life if we rebuild
him and pour revival fluid on him.

04:40.010 --> 04:41.800
Oh, Kohaku...

04:41.800 --> 04:44.710
I think you've got a statue headed your way.

04:45.310 --> 04:47.800
Don't worry about it. For now...

04:46.040 --> 04:47.800
Wait, you have a plan?

04:50.700 --> 04:52.890
You there, little girl...

04:52.890 --> 04:55.290
Kohaku-chan, was it?

04:55.290 --> 04:57.430
What's wrong? Can't you break it?

04:58.400 --> 05:01.070
Are <i>you</i> the intruder?

05:17.210 --> 05:20.250
Ryusui!

05:24.650 --> 05:26.430
Destroyed, as ordered.

05:26.930 --> 05:28.390
Problem?

05:28.620 --> 05:30.370
No, I think I'm good.

05:30.370 --> 05:34.610
Oh, look at you, Kohaku-chan,
making such a mess!

05:34.610 --> 05:36.640
I'll clean it up for you.

05:37.620 --> 05:38.870
Nothing to worry about.

05:38.870 --> 05:40.390
Without Yuzuriha here,

05:40.390 --> 05:43.310
we wouldn't be able to restore him
if they smashed him into dust.

05:43.310 --> 05:45.780
I disassembled him cleanly with my hands.

05:48.760 --> 05:52.370
Hey, Kohaku and them sent
us a bunch of stuff.

05:54.730 --> 05:57.180
Hey, there's our first delivery!

05:59.510 --> 06:01.960
D-Don't tell me...

06:02.370 --> 06:06.590
Are they going to send us Ryusui-chan
piece by piece with the Nezumini 4WDs?

06:07.960 --> 06:10.470
What else could they do?

06:10.470 --> 06:14.330
We're using the petrification beam
to make a piecemeal prison escape.

06:14.330 --> 06:17.950
I've always known you were
ridiculously rational, but...

06:17.950 --> 06:18.880
But still...

06:18.880 --> 06:22.360
You're practically psycho at this point!

06:24.910 --> 06:27.610
Why are there so many rats today?!

06:27.610 --> 06:28.900
I'm sorry!

06:28.900 --> 06:32.260
I'm sure Kohaku-chan will catch all of them.

06:34.280 --> 06:36.290
Knowing Ryusui...

06:38.990 --> 06:41.670
Well done dismembering me!

06:41.670 --> 06:42.850
Thanks to you,

06:42.850 --> 06:47.090
I've earned the trophy of becoming
the first person to be revived twice!

06:47.520 --> 06:48.710
Is probably what he's saying.

06:48.710 --> 06:50.320
You're delusional!

06:50.320 --> 06:52.500
Honestly, he might actually say that.

06:57.940 --> 07:01.390
Ryusui was the one who saved me.

07:01.930 --> 07:07.810
The enemy took his favorite captain's hat,
so I made him one out of paper.

07:33.470 --> 07:34.410
Huh?

07:34.410 --> 07:36.080
What is this?

07:36.080 --> 07:39.450
Where's the usual "crackle crackle"?

07:40.100 --> 07:43.810
Yeah, after a few thousand years,

07:43.810 --> 07:47.980
the surface is too weathered for the skin
to turn back into cells, and it falls off.

07:47.980 --> 07:51.540
But for him, it's only been a few days,
so it hasn't weathered one bit.

07:51.540 --> 07:55.280
What we're witnessing now is the
<i>real</i> de-petrification reaction.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.870
Appreciated, everyone!

08:08.870 --> 08:10.100
Thanks to you,

08:10.100 --> 08:14.090
I've earned the trophy of becoming
the first person to be revived twice!

08:14.300 --> 08:16.010
Ryusui!

08:16.720 --> 08:18.550
Though, I'm not sure I'm the first.

08:18.550 --> 08:20.130
You're the first.

08:21.310 --> 08:22.810
Which means...

08:28.150 --> 08:30.150
It's statues we want right now!

08:30.150 --> 08:31.140
Am I right?

08:31.140 --> 08:32.300
Obviously.

08:32.300 --> 08:33.990
This dude catches on fast.

08:34.200 --> 08:35.660
Ryusui is
revived!!

08:37.090 --> 08:38.620
Well done, Suika!

08:39.030 --> 08:42.210
You were the lone survivor
on the battlefield.

08:42.210 --> 08:45.940
You're already an accomplished
warrior of the Kingdom of Science.

08:49.430 --> 08:51.590
I have a rough idea of the current situation.

08:51.950 --> 08:53.960
You can always trust a sailor's instincts.

08:54.600 --> 08:57.370
We're catching the petrification weapon
as soon as the enemy tosses it.

08:57.370 --> 08:59.840
An aerial battle. Am I right?

08:59.530 --> 09:01.310
Bam!

09:00.440 --> 09:01.310
Am I right?!

09:01.310 --> 09:03.630
Nope!

09:01.620 --> 09:04.430
Drone!!

09:06.730 --> 09:11.050
It's such a wild plan, even the greed
master Ryusui-chan is speechless!

09:11.050 --> 09:11.970
No...

09:12.360 --> 09:13.190
I like it.

09:13.740 --> 09:15.410
Be faithful to your wants!

09:15.410 --> 09:17.940
That's what makes the Kingdom
of Science what it is!

09:21.880 --> 09:25.590
Is it just me, or is the
security kinda crazy?

09:25.590 --> 09:28.920
Even Ibara and the top
warrior Mozu are there!

09:30.490 --> 09:35.050
They're ten billion percent suspicious
that there's an intruder among them.

09:35.470 --> 09:38.240
We aren't getting a millimeter closer.

09:38.240 --> 09:40.920
H-How about we sneak in late at night?

09:40.920 --> 09:43.260
We can't search the sea
floor without daylight.

09:43.260 --> 09:45.490
And they'll catch us when we rise to breathe.

09:46.040 --> 09:46.770
Which means...

09:47.770 --> 09:49.350
we'll have to dive now!

09:49.350 --> 09:51.190
Let's go, Soyuz!

09:51.190 --> 09:52.440
That was a quick decision!

09:53.710 --> 09:59.890
So... I guess you and I were never even
considered useful for physical tasks.

10:14.170 --> 10:16.110
Yeah, of course that that would happen.

10:16.110 --> 10:17.760
No way you could dive that long.

10:17.760 --> 10:21.940
Then it's time for a fun southern
island scuba diving trip.

10:22.470 --> 10:24.640
We're making oxygen tanks.

10:36.740 --> 10:39.480
Why are you gleefully
taking apart the lab car?!

10:39.480 --> 10:41.870
We don't have time to build
the tanks from scratch.

10:41.870 --> 10:44.660
So we're reusing some parts.

10:45.540 --> 10:47.030
A pipe from the lab car.

10:47.030 --> 10:48.640
It's just a steel pipe.

10:48.640 --> 10:50.790
All right! I need a lid!

10:50.790 --> 10:53.130
Isn't that a bit too half-assed?!

10:54.540 --> 10:56.760
Don't tell me...

10:56.760 --> 10:59.000
You're using that as the oxygen cylinder?

10:59.000 --> 11:00.750
Can it survive the air pressure?

11:00.750 --> 11:02.960
Yeah, I've tried it before.

11:02.960 --> 11:06.770
Seal the flanges and solder
the seams tightly shut,

11:06.770 --> 11:09.250
and they'll just barely hold up
to about 100 atmospheres.

11:09.250 --> 11:11.400
Although it blew up a month later.

11:11.630 --> 11:15.580
I dunno what to think,
but then again, Senku-chan

11:15.580 --> 11:18.980
used to build hobby rocket engines and stuff.

11:21.990 --> 11:25.000
This is that "oxygen tank" thing?

11:25.000 --> 11:27.690
It looks like ass. Even for us.

11:27.690 --> 11:30.950
Unlike craftsman Kaseki-sama,
I'm just an amateur.

11:30.950 --> 11:33.330
The clunky look makes it endearing.

11:33.330 --> 11:35.940
We're gonna need a hella clunky pump, too.

11:35.940 --> 11:38.330
Maybe we can use the engine
pistons or something.

11:39.340 --> 11:42.030
He's taking it all apart!

11:42.030 --> 11:45.220
I'm swiping the regulator
to cap off the tank.

11:45.220 --> 11:46.870
You're going to make Kaseki-chan cry.

11:46.870 --> 11:49.470
My dear lab car!

11:50.000 --> 11:52.110
Don't underestimate Kaseki.

11:52.110 --> 11:55.560
He can just rebuild all of it once he's back.

11:55.810 --> 11:58.320
You're right.

11:58.550 --> 12:01.990
You two make yourselves
sound all sentimental,

12:02.200 --> 12:05.050
but Kaseki-chan's going
to be the one suffering!

12:06.920 --> 12:11.290
Now, all that's left is to shove
some air into it with the pump.

12:11.290 --> 12:12.840
Um...

12:12.840 --> 12:15.610
I have a bad feeling... A <i>really</i> bad feeling...

12:15.610 --> 12:20.510
Is this going to be another one of those
Kingdom of Science manual labor things?

12:21.640 --> 12:25.370
It's light enough that
even I can do it, though.

12:25.370 --> 12:26.980
No way.

12:27.660 --> 12:29.130
Oh, you're right.

12:29.130 --> 12:30.520
I was totally expecting...

12:30.520 --> 12:31.950
Yeah, at first.

12:30.620 --> 12:35.600
2 atm

12:31.950 --> 12:35.120
It's about the same as a bike pump
up to around two atmospheres.

12:38.020 --> 12:41.320
10 atm

12:47.840 --> 12:49.280
50 atm

12:50.020 --> 12:51.050
Suika!

12:51.050 --> 12:54.330
Storing air also means storing heat.

12:54.330 --> 12:56.970
The pump's gonna heat up
like crazy and explode.

12:56.970 --> 12:58.340
Dump water on it!

12:58.340 --> 12:59.700
Got it!

13:01.590 --> 13:05.590
H-How much longer are we doing this?

13:05.590 --> 13:07.050
Let's see...

13:07.050 --> 13:09.030
Based on its capacity...

13:09.380 --> 13:13.060
Maybe about five hours...
times the number of pumps we have.

13:13.060 --> 13:16.560
I knew it!

13:16.560 --> 13:19.060
10 hours later

13:24.590 --> 13:27.320
Th-The air pump blew up!

13:27.320 --> 13:29.700
It's over!

13:32.340 --> 13:34.490
No, it's perfect.

13:34.490 --> 13:36.610
We just need two of them.

13:46.010 --> 13:48.390
Oxygen tanks
acquired!!

13:48.390 --> 13:49.820
W-Wow.

13:49.820 --> 13:52.520
We're really breathing underwater.

14:03.830 --> 14:06.750
How long are those tanks going to last?

14:06.750 --> 14:10.250
It depends on the depth, but probably about...

14:10.250 --> 14:11.740
ten minutes.

14:11.740 --> 14:13.040
That's it?!

14:15.040 --> 14:17.610
We spent ten hours pumping like crazy.

14:17.610 --> 14:21.210
And the pumpy thing blew up already.

14:21.470 --> 14:23.990
They're our first and last oxygen tanks.

14:23.990 --> 14:26.210
It's do-or-die in ten minutes.

14:26.980 --> 14:30.720
We have to find Kaseki at
the bottom and save him.

14:31.150 --> 14:33.530
Ten minutes isn't long enough.

14:33.530 --> 14:36.060
We need some kind of hint.

14:39.800 --> 14:46.400
The enemy dropped the statues from the
surface at this speed, in that direction.

14:49.940 --> 14:52.170
How can you reconstruct
the situation that clearly?

14:52.170 --> 14:54.580
You're impressive, Soyuz.

14:55.370 --> 14:56.120
In fact...

14:56.870 --> 15:01.780
Come to think of it, having memories of
your infancy is no ordinary feat, either.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.670
But thanks.

15:05.670 --> 15:07.670
That information is worth a million!

15:09.200 --> 15:12.650
I believe in Ryusui. He'll find everyone.

15:13.200 --> 15:17.080
He knows the sea better than anyone!

15:19.900 --> 15:21.480
This is...

15:28.110 --> 15:29.860
It's a reef current.

15:29.860 --> 15:33.040
A violent rip current that occurs
at the edges of coral reefs.

15:33.950 --> 15:38.610
Which must mean all the pieces
were carried by this current.

15:43.920 --> 15:45.120
Everyone!

15:45.120 --> 15:48.290
My trusty sailors of the
Science Vessel Perseus!

15:48.290 --> 15:51.710
Well done sticking it out in this darkness!

15:52.240 --> 15:54.010
I'm giving you a work bonus.

15:54.010 --> 15:56.810
I promise all of you a massive drago reward!

16:08.970 --> 16:10.550
Three jellyfish!

16:11.630 --> 16:12.780
1 jellyfish: found a few people
2 jellyfish: found just Kaseki
3 jellyfish: found everyone

16:12.780 --> 16:14.610
3 jellyfish: found everyone

16:14.850 --> 16:16.820
They've found everyone!

16:16.820 --> 16:18.370
Awesome!

16:18.370 --> 16:21.440
Now we can revive everyone!

16:21.440 --> 16:25.490
Yeah, but don't forget our priorities.

16:25.490 --> 16:28.840
If we don't wake up Kaseki the
craftsman first, we're screwed.

16:29.410 --> 16:31.730
We don't have any more oxygen tanks.

16:31.730 --> 16:34.070
This is our only shot at this rescue dive.

16:35.120 --> 16:37.930
First, Kaseki, I want you!

17:01.120 --> 17:03.110
He's completely buried.

17:03.110 --> 17:03.990
Yeah...

17:03.990 --> 17:05.920
He won't budge at all.

17:07.590 --> 17:12.240
Isn't it about time they signal
for us to pull them up?

17:12.240 --> 17:14.130
They haven't said anything.

17:14.470 --> 17:16.130
Their remaining air...

17:16.430 --> 17:19.500
The average male breathes
15 liters per minute.

17:19.500 --> 17:22.080
Assuming that's an average
of 20 based on their activity,

17:22.080 --> 17:24.890
and the 10-liter tank size and
a starting pressure of 70...

17:25.480 --> 17:27.650
The question is their depth.

17:27.650 --> 17:31.480
Estimating from where the jellyfish
came up and the behavior of the rope,

17:31.480 --> 17:33.530
they're roughly 20 meters down.

17:36.110 --> 17:38.700
We've got four minutes of oxygen left.

17:39.160 --> 17:40.660
I-It's no use.

17:40.660 --> 17:42.000
He's stuck in the mud.

17:42.000 --> 17:43.750
It'll take hours to dig him out.

17:44.110 --> 17:47.590
But without Kaseki, we can't
make any more oxygen tanks.

17:47.590 --> 17:49.560
We can never come back.

17:49.560 --> 17:52.460
This is our only chance!

17:52.890 --> 17:55.470
We absolutely must bring
Kaseki back to the surface!

17:56.180 --> 18:00.900
When your strength isn't enough,
you have to use the strength of your crew.

18:00.900 --> 18:03.020
That's a leader's job!

18:03.020 --> 18:04.100
Am I right?

18:06.490 --> 18:07.960
They're signaling us!

18:07.960 --> 18:11.560
Huh? But isn't there something weird
about how they're tugging the rope?

18:11.560 --> 18:13.450
It might be some kind of message.

18:13.450 --> 18:16.110
Tuuug, tuuug, tug, tug...

18:17.450 --> 18:18.660
Morse code!

18:18.660 --> 18:20.590
Dash, dash, dot, dot...

18:20.590 --> 18:21.960
Is that a Z?

18:21.960 --> 18:24.610
Do they have any idea how
long it'll take to send

18:24.610 --> 18:26.290
a message over the safety rope?

18:26.290 --> 18:27.600
It's fine.

18:27.600 --> 18:29.530
I'm sure it won't be that long.

18:29.530 --> 18:32.360
We're buddies. We don't need words.

18:33.380 --> 18:36.950
We'd just told Ryusui-chan
that we don't have time.

18:36.950 --> 18:39.310
Which means there's something they want.

18:39.310 --> 18:42.350
We're in a hurry, so there's
no way it's a sentence.

18:42.350 --> 18:43.860
It's a word.

18:43.860 --> 18:47.000
But there are only a few
words that start with Z.

18:47.000 --> 18:47.680
Zoo.

18:47.680 --> 18:48.550
Zebra.

18:48.550 --> 18:49.390
Zipper.

18:49.390 --> 18:50.480
Zinc.

18:50.480 --> 18:51.950
None of those fit.

18:51.950 --> 18:54.410
Which means it's Japanese Morse code.

18:54.410 --> 18:56.140
Dash, dash, dot, dot.

18:55.290 --> 18:59.650
Fu

18:56.140 --> 18:56.940
"Fu."

18:56.940 --> 18:59.650
"I need something that starts with 'fu'"!

19:01.810 --> 19:03.240
Revival fluid!

19:09.350 --> 19:10.120
They're fast.

19:19.510 --> 19:21.590
I-I see!

19:21.590 --> 19:24.090
If we can wake up Taiju,
who's got the most power,

19:24.090 --> 19:25.980
he might be able to pull
Kaseki's statue out.

19:27.020 --> 19:28.410
But, Ryusui...

19:28.410 --> 19:32.090
You can't pour revival
fluid on him underwater.

19:32.090 --> 19:33.400
How can you...

19:41.020 --> 19:44.940
I made some air that's the same
as the outside air using the pump.

19:44.940 --> 19:46.990
I'm spraying the revival
fluid on him from below.

19:47.640 --> 19:50.220
He made that decision in this brief instant?

19:50.220 --> 19:52.180
To use the last of his oxygen?

19:53.710 --> 19:54.890
Oh, no!

19:54.890 --> 19:56.540
He's missing part of his arm.

19:56.830 --> 19:58.590
If we revive him now...

20:03.000 --> 20:06.100
How could he tell at first glance
that that was Taiju's arm?

20:07.050 --> 20:10.810
Did he remember what it looked
like when everyone was petrified?

20:11.600 --> 20:13.650
Good job, Soyuz!

20:37.000 --> 20:38.460
Taiju is
revived!!

20:37.230 --> 20:39.280
I'm awake, of course!

20:40.990 --> 20:42.870
Y-Yeah, that was bound to happen!

20:42.870 --> 20:43.630
Sorry!

20:43.630 --> 20:46.140
Imagine waking up and you're
suddenly underwater...

20:46.370 --> 20:51.390
I have to relay to Taiju the current
situation and what we need of him quickly.

20:51.390 --> 20:54.240
I need only to connect the space
between me and Taiju with air!

20:54.960 --> 20:56.020
Get Kaseki!

20:56.020 --> 20:58.230
We're reviving Kaseki first!

21:07.570 --> 21:10.150
I'll manage on that single breath.

21:10.150 --> 21:12.340
You have to breathe, too, Ryusui.

21:12.650 --> 21:15.080
Talking isn't what's important!

21:15.320 --> 21:16.340
We're a team.

21:16.340 --> 21:18.990
We can communicate without
words, just with our hearts!

21:23.870 --> 21:25.920
Not that I've got any reason to believe that!

21:25.920 --> 21:29.050
No, you're absolutely right, Taiju.

21:30.290 --> 21:31.960
I hear your heart.

21:52.650 --> 21:55.880
We're getting close to the uh-oh time limit.

21:57.060 --> 21:57.870
Pull them up!

22:03.140 --> 22:05.130
